1. Grant of Rights

Subject to the conditions below, permission is hereby granted, free of
charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated
documentation files (the "Software"), to use, copy, modify, merge,
publish, distribute, sublicense, and sell copies of the Software or any
derivative work.

2. Copyleft / Source Availability

Anyone who distributes, conveys, makes downloadable, or otherwise
provides a third party with an executable copy of the Software or any
derivative work — whether modified or unmodified, and whether or not
for commercial purposes — including but not limited to publishing a
UserScript, providing an install link, or listing it in a plugin
manager, must:

  a. provide, or provide access to, the complete corresponding
     human-readable source code, under terms no more burdensome to
     obtain than those for the executable copy itself;
  b. license that source code and derivative work to downstream
     recipients under the same terms as this license, so they receive
     the same rights you did;
  c. not impose any further restriction on a downstream recipient's
     exercise of the rights granted by this license.

3. Attribution

Any copy or derivative work of the Software, in whole or in substantial
part, must:

  a. retain this license notice in full;
  b. clearly credit the original author, Likolisu, and include a link
     to the source repository (https://github.com/awdrrawd/BC-AEE);
  c. clearly credit contributors InkerBot
     (https://github.com/InkerBot) and Tao MUSE (https://github.com/heitaoplay).

This attribution must be presented in a place a user would reasonably
find it, such as a README, an "About" page, a copyright notice section,
or a prominent location on the release or product page.

4. Substantial Modification Required for Commercial Use

To use the Software or any derivative work for any commercial purpose
(including but not limited to selling copies, offering it as part of a
paid subscription or paid membership content, monetizing it through
advertising, or including it as part of a paid service), in addition to
the source-availability obligation in Section 2, the derivative work
must constitute a **Substantial Modification** of the Software — not
merely a small, cosmetic, or incremental change layered on top of the
original skeleton.

4.1 Test

The core test for a Substantial Modification is whether a reasonable
user or developer would regard the derivative work as "a new product
that builds on AEE but has developed its own independent value and
functionality," rather than "AEE with one or two small features bolted
on and sold for profit." Relevant factors include, without limitation:

  a. Functionality: the addition of genuinely new core features or
     modules that represent substantial engineering effort, rather than
     parameter tweaks, re-skinning, or simple toggles on existing
     features;
  b. Codebase: meaningful refactoring or replacement of core logic
     (e.g. the layer engine, rendering pipeline, data structures, or
     controller architecture), rather than changes limited to styling,
     copy text, variable names, or configuration files;
  c. Overall proportion: the Software's original code/logic should not
     constitute the overwhelming majority, or the sole selling point,
     of the resulting product.

4.2 Non-Exhaustive Examples That Do NOT Qualify

The following, without more, generally do NOT constitute a Substantial
Modification and may not be used as the basis for commercial use:

  - Renaming, re-icon-ing, or re-theming the UI;
  - Translating text or adjusting default values/settings;
  - Adding only one or two minor features while keeping the rest of the
    skeleton and logic unchanged;
  - Repackaging the Software under a different loader or install
    method without changing its substance;
  - Removing or hiding the attribution required by this license.

4.3 When in Doubt

If you are unsure whether a particular modification meets the
Substantial Modification threshold, contact the original author,
Likolisu, before commercializing it, or use, modify, and distribute the
Software on a non-commercial basis instead (non-commercial use is not
subject to this Section, but remains subject to Sections 2 and 3).

5. Same License for Derivatives

Any derivative work distributed under this license must be licensed to
downstream recipients under **these same terms** — it may not be
relicensed under different terms, and none of the obligations in this
license may be removed.

6. Disclaimer of Warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF
MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.
IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY
CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT,
TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE
SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
